{"chunk_id": "cda40b5c737c", "text": "At the climax of Yudhishthira\u2019s great sacrifice, sages, kings, and Brahmanas gather in the inner enclosure, creating a scene likened to a divine assembly in Brahma\u2019s heaven. The sage Narada observes the gathering and reflects on a cosmic secret: many of the warriors present are incarnations of gods destined to destroy one another on earth as part of Narayana\u2019s plan. Recognizing Krishna as that divine presence living among men, Narada sits in awe. Following ritual custom, Bhishma instructs Yudhishthira to offer the first ceremonial Arghya\u2014the highest honor\u2014to the most worthy guest. Bhishma declares Krishna supreme among them, and Sahadeva presents the offering. Krishna accepts it, but the proud king Sisupala erupts in anger, denouncing the choice and publicly insulting both Bhishma and Yudhishthira, setting the stage for a major conflict.\nAt Yudhishthira\u2019s sacrifice Bhishma awards the first Arghya to Krishna, provoking Sisupala to angrily denounce the honor before the assembled kings.\nThemes: ritual honor, divine incarnation, courtly dispute, Krishna\u2019s supremacy, political tension", "vector": [0.004590887576341629, -0.022060370072722435, -0.012356217950582504, -0.0026889005675911903, -0.00725969672203064, 0.0217656958848238, -0.021993398666381836, -0.0108158765360713, -0.016086524352431297, -0.019796738401055336, 0.01524268463253975, 0.009429569356143475, 0.004215847700834274, -0.00315100303851068, -0.011827144771814346, -0.008471878245472908, 0.04200444370508194, 0.00010453812865307555, 0.027310926467180252, -0.006238383240997791, -0.012215577997267246, 0.0020945295691490173, -0.008545546792447567, 0.024123087525367737, -0.01584542728960514, 0.02885126695036888, 0.02110937610268593, -0.01650174707174301, 0.013755920343101025, -0.010286802425980568, -0.010963213630020618, -0.0008823478128761053, -0.001292547443881631, 0.010755602270364761, -0.040932901203632355, -0.012188789434731007, 0.000402